JT	00	INFO	FLATF	01:08:19.08	Outgoing command: Que Body(OC1COD1   SVR       OFI             \ofa:M\ofc:PCR\ofcl:Post-Case Reconciliation\ofd:Disable\ofl:Post-Case Reconciliation Support\ofn:If enabled a new button will be available on the patient function screen. This button will initiate the PCR process. Items in anesthesia supply drawers are excluded. If disabled, this button will not be shown and PCR will not be available. When enabled, all wastes for PCR eligible items must be completed via the PCR process. \ofo:POSTCASERECONCILIATION\ofr:Enable;Disable\oft:L\ofv:Disable\osi:OC1COD1)
JT	00	INFO	FLATF	01:08:19.48	Outgoing command: Que Body(OC1COD1   SVR       OFI             \ofa:M\ofc:PCR\ofcl:Post-Case Reconciliation\ofd:Enable\ofl:Access Return Bin\ofn:If enabled the Case Complete button on the PCR screen will access the return bin, if possible. If disabled the return bin will not be accessed from the PCR screen, even if one is available.\ofo:POSTCASERETURNBIN\ofr:Enable;Disable\oft:L\ofv:Enable\osi:OC1COD1)
JT	00	INFO	FLATF	01:08:19.82	Outgoing command: Que Body(OC1COD1   SVR       OFI             \ofa:M\ofc:PCR\ofcl:Post-Case Reconciliation\ofd:Enable\ofl:Print Receipt\ofn:If enabled the Case Complete button on the PCR screen will generate a receipt of the current PCR activity, if possible. If disabled no receipt will be printed from the PCR screen, even if a printer is available.\ofo:POSTCASERECEIPT\ofr:Enable;Disable\oft:L\ofv:Disable\osi:OC1COD1)
JT	00	INFO	FLATF	01:08:21.33	Outgoing command: Que Body(OC1COD1   SVR       OFI             \ofa:M\ofc:PCR\ofcl:Post-Case Reconciliation\ofd:Enable\ofl:Waste Witness Rules\ofn:If enabled existing rules will determine if a witness will be required to as part of the PCR.  If disabled, no witness is required for PCR even if one or more items on the PCR list normally require a waste witness. \ofo:POSTCASEWITNESS\ofr:Enable;Disable\oft:L\ofv:Disable\osi:OC1COD1)
JT	00	INFO	FLATF	01:08:21.72	Outgoing command: Que Body(OC1COD1   SVR       OFI             \ofa:M\ofc:PCR\ofcl:Post-Case Reconciliation\ofd:Enable\ofl:Allow Standard Waste of Meds\ofn:If enabled, PCR users can waste non-PCR items using the standard waste meds function and/or waste partial dose at time of issue. If disabled, the waste meds button is not shown for PCR users and waste partial dose at time of issue is not available. When disabled these users can only waste items via PCR. \ofo:POSTCASEALLOWSTDWASTE\ofr:Enable;Disable\oft:L\ofv:Enable\osi:OC1COD1)
JT	00	INFO	FLATF	01:08:21.73	Outgoing command: Que Body(OC1COD1   SVR       OFI             \ofa:M\ofc:PCR\ofcl:Post-Case Reconciliation\ofd:Enable\ofl:Reminder to Complete Return Message\ofn:If enabled, a message is shown when PCR is initiated reminding the user to complete returns prior to PCR. If disabled, no message is shown, the user proceeds directly to the PCR screen.\ofo:POSTCASERETURNMESSAGE\ofr:Enable;Disable\oft:L\ofv:Disable\osi:OC1COD1)
JT	00	INFO	FLATF	01:08:21.86	Outgoing command: Que Body(OC1COD1   SVR       OFI             \ofa:M\ofc:PCR\ofcl:Post-Case Reconciliation\ofd:Enable\ofl:Blank or All Zero Waste Message\ofn:If enabled, a message is shown when the user attempts to complete the case for a blank waste and/or all zero waste on the PCR screen. If disabled, no message is shown due to a blank waste or all zero waste on case complete.\ofo:POSTCASEBLANKZEROWASTEMESSAGE\ofr:Enable;Disable\oft:L\ofv:Enable\osi:OC1COD1)
JT	00	INFO	FLATF	01:08:22.08	Outgoing command: Que Body(OC1COD1   SVR       OFI             \ofa:M\ofc:PCR\ofcl:Post-Case Reconciliation\ofd:No\ofl:Waste Witness Required for All Zero Waste\ofn:When enabled, a witness is required for all zero waste amount when item waste-witness is also enabled and (waste witness rules) is enabled for PCR\ofo:POSTCASEZEROWASTEWITNESS\ofr:Yes;No\oft:L\ofv:Yes\osi:OC1COD1)
JT	00	INFO	FLATF	01:08:22.41	Outgoing command: Que Body(OC1COD1   SVR       OFI             \ofa:M\ofc:PCR\ofcl:Post-Case Reconciliation\ofd:Disable\ofl:Access Return Bin for All Zero Waste\ofn:When enabled, the Case Complete button on the PCR screen will acess the return bin for all zero waste, when possible. When disabled, the return bin will not be accessible from PCR screen for all zero waste, even if one is available.\ofo:POSTCASEZEROWASTEACCESSRETURNBIN\ofr:Enable;Disable\oft:L\ofv:Enable\osi:OC1COD1)
